# Minimalist scrollbars

Child of `page-architecture.mdc` (same folder). SoilGood is editorial and phone-first. Scrollbars must stay **thin and quiet** — overlay, no track, auto-hide while idle. Do not ship the thick Windows/Chrome default.

Set this **once** in theme / `web/` CSS. Do not restyle scrollbars per page.

## Look
- **Thickness:** ~4–6px (thumb only).
- **Track:** transparent (no gray gutter).
- **Thumb:** muted charcoal/outline, ~28% opacity; slightly stronger on hover. Not primary green.
- **Radius:** ~8px (rounded rectangle, not a capsule).
- **Visibility:** show while scrolling; hide when idle. Never a permanent fat bar.
- **Horizontal strips** (forecast, chips): no persistent bar — swipe/trackpad only.

## Flutter (all platforms, including Chrome)

```dart
scrollbarTheme: ScrollbarThemeData(
  thickness: const WidgetStatePropertyAll(4),
  radius: const Radius.circular(8),
  thumbColor: WidgetStatePropertyAll(
    AppColors.textSecondary.withValues(alpha: 0.28),
  ),
  trackVisibility: const WidgetStatePropertyAll(false),
  thumbVisibility: const WidgetStatePropertyAll(false),
  interactive: true,
),
```

Do not wrap every `ListView` in a custom `Scrollbar`. Theme covers it. Do not set `scrollBehavior` to hide bars entirely on web — farmers still need a scroll cue.

## Flutter web (`web/index.html` or a linked CSS)

Browser overflow (html/body) is **not** themed by Flutter. Add:

```css
html { scrollbar-width: thin; scrollbar-color: rgba(74, 78, 74, 0.35) transparent; }
::-webkit-scrollbar { width: 6px; height: 6px; }
::-webkit-scrollbar-track { background: transparent; }
::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb {
  background: rgba(74, 78, 74, 0.28);
  border-radius: 8px;
}
```

## Do not
- Thick 12–16px OS/Material bars
- Colored primary-green thumbs
- Always-visible track
- `display: none` on all scrollbars (no way to see leftover content on web)
